('s-ra-7', 'speaking-read-aloud', '{"text":"Historians studying trade networks in the ancient world have found evidence of goods travelling thousands of kilometres long before any single empire controlled the entire route."}'::jsonb),
('s-ra-8', 'speaking-read-aloud', '{"text":"Urban planners are increasingly designing neighborhoods around pedestrians and cyclists rather than cars, hoping to reduce both traffic congestion and carbon emissions."}'::jsonb),
